","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a23217175515970826202db7c4a2c5b356155eba6db718f8878d33f7e2e005cd","event_uuid":"a3fecbdf-7dad-4c70-9861-b2118a94b6ec","position":{"commit_sha":"c62ebb810887df95a9c6275cb421edc10aae9d2d","position":"1786565017475814338-a3fecbdf-7dad-4c70-9861-b2118a94b6ec"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786509669621877001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ea184145-d60c-40e0-bddd-a18f1d55612b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2030-2d8e-73e6-4bf9"},{"link_uuid":"f380fd81-54cc-43ab-91f6-636b922defd6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4a89-e634-36b3-4bf6"},{"link_uuid":"a3fecbdf-7dad-4c70-9861-b2118a94b6ec","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bdd2-333a-f5b3-4055"}],"description":"# s3 doctor should fold bundle heads into the published ref, not the worktree HEAD\n\n## Context\n\nSplit out of bug `gnarled-acardiac-bettong` (landed as Gerrit 1628), which proved the defect and\nclosed the silent-corruption door with a loud refusal. This ticket is the proper fix that\nrefusal stands in for, and retires the refusal.\n\nToday `_fold_heads` (`src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py:232-261`) merges every fetched bundle head\ninto the tracker WORKTREE's HEAD with `git merge` and returns `git rev-parse HEAD`. Because\n`git merge` only merges into the checked-out branch, the heal's result is a function of whatever\nbranch the tracker happens to be on. `_require_tracker_on_ref` (`s3_doctor.py:167-195`) therefore\nrefuses the heal outright whenever `current_branch != ref` (detached HEAD included), so the\ndoctor is SAFE but cannot heal such a tracker at all.\n\n## Premise validated against origin/main (cc69cc1179)\n\n- The guard and its \"retires with envious-metal-budgie\" docstring are present at\n  `s3_doctor.py:167-195`; `_heal_locked` calls it at `s3_doctor.py:136`.\n- `_publish_and_prune` (`s3_doctor.py:264-317`) now relies on that guard: its docstring records\n  that the `git branch -f` fallback was removed, and it bundles `HEAD` + `refs/heads/<ref>` at\n  `s3_doctor.py:285`.\n- Regression floor is GREEN today: `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py` +\n  `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py` = 18 passed, 1 skipped.\n\n## Mechanism decision (experimentally settled, not assumed)\n\nThe ticket left the mechanism open (`merge-tree`/`commit-tree` vs a scratch worktree). Probed\nboth concerns on Git 2.55 in a throwaway repo shaped like the tracker:\n\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree A B` DOES honour the tracker's configured `ours` driver\n  (`merge.ours.driver=true`, set by `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:559`) together with the\n  tickets-branch `.gitattributes` `.bridge_state/* merge=ours` line\n  (`_commands/init.py:62`). It produced a tree byte-identical to the worktree `git merge` on the\n  same inputs, and it CONFLICTS identically when the driver is absent. So the merge policy AC is\n  satisfiable without a worktree.\n- A real content conflict exits non-zero and names the conflicted paths — and, unlike `git\n  merge`, leaves NO worktree/index state, so no `merge --abort` is needed.\n- `git commit-tree <tree> -p <ref-tip> -p <head>` builds the 2-parent merge commit; unrelated\n  histories need `--allow-unrelated-histories` on `merge-tree`. That flag is NOT a new version\n  requirement: git-merge-tree(1) documents both `--write-tree` and `--allow-unrelated-histories`\n  as of 2.38.0 (checked against the 2.38.0 manual page), which is exactly the floor the repo\n  already enforces — so no version fallback is needed and none is planned.\n\nA scratch worktree was rejected: it costs a full checkout of the event tree on every heal.\n`merge-tree` needs no checkout and never touches the worktree. Git floor is already 2.38 for\n`merge-tree --write-tree` (README.md:143-147, `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py`).\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Rewrite `_fold_heads` (`s3_doctor.py:232-261`)** to fold into the published ref, not HEAD:\n   start from `refs/heads/<ref>`'s tip; for each head ref, skip if already an ancestor of the\n   running tip; else `git merge-tree --write-tree [--allow-unrelated-histories] <tip> <head>`\n   then `git commit-tree <tree> -p <tip> -p <head> -m \"Merge <head> (s3 doctor auto-heal of ref\n   <ref>)\"`. A non-zero `merge-tree` still raises `S3DoctorConflict` with the same message shape\n   (the existing hint carrying `fsck-recover` is preserved). Keep the existing write lock and the\n   iterated 2-parent shape. Both flags are inside the repo's existing 2.38 Git floor, so no\n   version probe or fallback path is introduced.\n2. **Move the ref (`_heal_locked`, `s3_doctor.py:136-143`)**: publish the folded sha onto\n   `refs/heads/<ref>` under the same lock. When `ref` is NOT checked out:\n   `git update-ref refs/heads/<ref> <merged> <old-tip>` — a compare-and-swap, so a concurrent\n   mover aborts the heal instead of clobbering. When `ref` IS the checked-out branch: `git reset\n   --hard <merged>`, so index and worktree stay consistent with the branch exactly as the old\n   `git merge` left them.\n3. **Replace the refusal guard**: delete `_require_tracker_on_ref` (`s3_doctor.py:167-195`) and\n   its call (`s3_doctor.py:136`). In its place, a much narrower pre-download guard: when `ref` IS\n   checked out and the worktree is dirty, refuse before downloading anything (today's `git merge`\n   already fails on a dirty worktree, later and less clearly — this keeps that refusal and makes\n   it early). A tracker on another branch or detached HEAD is no longer refused at all.\n4. **Fix `_publish_and_prune` (`s3_doctor.py:264-317`)**: its docstring's \"guard has established\n   ref IS the checked-out branch\" reasoning is retired. Bundle `refs/heads/<ref>` explicitly\n   rather than relying on `HEAD` agreeing (`s3_doctor.py:285`); off-branch, HEAD no longer names\n   the merged tip.\n5. **Tests** (`tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py`): convert the three refusal tests\n   (`:206`, `:235`, `:251`) into HEAL tests — a side-branch tracker and a detached-HEAD tracker\n   both heal losslessly, and no commit reachable only from the side branch becomes reachable from\n   the published ref. Keep `:275` (single-bundle no-op off the ref). Add: the side branch and the\n   worktree HEAD are UNMOVED by an off-branch heal; the dirty-worktree refusal; and an\n   on-branch heal still advances HEAD/index/worktree.\n6. **Add the missing `merge=ours` regression.** The merge-policy AC has NO existing coverage:\n   grep for `merge=ours` / `bridge_state` across `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor*.py` and\n   `s3_doctor_harness.py` returns nothing, and the harness builds a bare `git init` tracker with\n   `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null` (`s3_doctor_harness.py:33-50`), so no `ours` driver and no\n   `.gitattributes` are in play today. Add a test that commits the tickets-branch\n   `.gitattributes` (`.bridge_state/* merge=ours`, as `_commands/init.py:62` writes) and sets\n   `merge.ours.driver=true` in the tracker (as `_commands/init.py:559` does), then folds two\n   heads that modify the SAME `.bridge_state/*` file differently: the heal must succeed with the\n   tracker's own side kept, not conflict. This test is written FIRST against today's `git merge`\n   fold, so it pins the policy the `merge-tree` rewrite must reproduce.\n   The real-conflict/no-delete behaviour at `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:109` must stay green\n   unchanged (line 81 is the unrelated-history union test, not a merge-policy test).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The heal folds heads into the published ref's tip regardless of the tracker's checked-out\n      branch.\n- [ ] No commit reachable only from the checked-out branch becomes reachable from the published\n      ref.\n- [ ] A new regression test proves the fold resolves a `.bridge_state/*` collision via\n      `merge=ours` (keeping the tracker's side) rather than conflicting; it passes on today's\n      fold and on the rewritten one.\n- [ ] A real content conflict raises `S3DoctorConflict` and deletes no bundle, rather than\n      resolving silently.\n- [ ] A tracker with a different branch checked out heals successfully.\n- [ ] A detached-HEAD tracker heals successfully.\n- [ ] `_require_tracker_on_ref` is deleted, and the off-branch/detached heals are proven by\n      tests that fail before this change.\n- [ ] After an on-branch heal, `git status --porcelain` in the tracker is empty (index and\n      worktree consistent with the moved ref).\n- [ ] After an off-branch heal, the checked-out branch's tip and the worktree are unchanged.\n- [ ] The 18 existing s3_doctor tests stay green.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py","reason":"rewrite _fold_heads to fold into the published ref via merge-tree/commit-tree; remove _require_tracker_on_ref; publish via update-ref/reset"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py","reason":"convert the three refusal tests into off-branch/detached heal tests; add worktree-state and dirty-worktree coverage"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4a89-e634-36b3-4bf6"],["relates_to","bdd2-333a-f5b3-4055"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ffee2a98-572d-4f65-ae92-420be30d1b57","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["s3_doctor"],"ticket_id":"bcfb-0d18-20fc-46b9","ticket_type":"task","title":"s3 doctor should fold bundle heads into the published ref, not the worktree HEAD","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["03c31830-9bbf-4f4f-ab70-26622dbd00ab","ea184145-d60c-40e0-bddd-a18f1d55612b","044e63fb-83be-4790-b5f5-9164ca3e2dc4","f92a2335-ba46-4ad0-8d3a-abb679ec2b22","f12d0ced-1340-4002-9cce-f0a3a8030819","33f32989-c0df-4e93-838f-ab4d0b8d85d0","bb58996b-ed1e-495a-b179-8ff0e177fc34","ffee2a98-572d-4f65-ae92-420be30d1b57","db88be16-cfcf-4811-8049-629e6022fa3f","f380fd81-54cc-43ab-91f6-636b922defd6","a3fecbdf-7dad-4c70-9861-b2118a94b6ec"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786565017475814339,"uuid":"af4543b1-62a0-48b5-9165-5e015d932d35"}